<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Fighter Role Play</h1>
<p>Most think of fighters as large and stupid. In truth, most fighters are not so much stupid or even uneducated, but rather are uncomplicated people with limited experience in the magics. The best fighter school is in Midgaard, but there are teachers of skills scattered across the world, although some have high standards before they will accept a student. Fighters study weapons thoroughly. Their main thrust is how to win a battle quickly whether in a bar or on the battlefield. Below are some suggestions to help you roleplay a fighter. If you should have any suggestions to add please use the <a cmd='#'>idea</a> command. Who knows, you may see it here!
</p>
<ul><li>Fighters come in all shapes, sizes and races. Some, like orcs, are predisposed to violence; for others, they have personal reasons. Some seek revenge, some are looking for someone, some just were of no use to their family on the farm, and could do little else but hone their fighting skills.</li>
<li>Some fighters find work as guards for merchants or caravans. This gives them pay and travel without the structure of an army or city guard position.</li>
<li>Some fighters work for the law. Many join the police guild in Midgaard.</li>
<li>The army is the answer for many fighters. Most join the one that is nearest to their home and travel from there. A few seek a specific one either because they believe in their cause or because they are far away.</li>
<li>Many barbarian or even country fighters mistrust magic, but trust in the power of prayer from a paladin or healer.</li>
<li>Fighters are frequently employed as leaders or second in command for adventuring parties. They act as shields to protect their charges most of the time.</li>
<li>Some fighters are in the profession just to fight.</li>
<li>Many fighters are murderers and enjoy the killing aspect of fighting; these bad men and women sometimes form bands to terrorize towns and even to form their own army to take over the world. So far none have totally succeeded.</li></ul>
<p><br />
